# What must NOT be committed.
#
# There was no .gitignore before, which is why build artefacts ended up tracked: the release
# zip of every version was committed, and so was the 38 MB Tailwind binary. A binary in a
# repository never shrinks — it stays in history whatever happens to the working tree — so
# the point of this file is to stop the NEXT one going in.

# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Release zips are produced by build-release.php from the source that is already committed.
# Committing them stores a second copy of the whole plugin per release, for ever.
*.zip

# --- Build tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Tailwind standalone binary. Not part of the plugin, and 38 MB — roughly twenty times
# everything else here put together. See the header of tailwind.config.js for where to get
# it if you need to rebuild the CSS.
tools/

# --- Credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `.vscode/sftp.json` holds deploy passwords in plain text. Two are already in this repo's
# history from before this rule existed, and history is why they have to be ROTATED rather
# than merely deleted — removing the file does not remove what it once contained.
.vscode/
.idea/

# Word's lock file for an open document. Appears whenever the guide is being read.
~$*

# --- Local noise ------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.sql
*.bak
*.orig
*~
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
._*
